  "question": "Finance risk model: $S(x)=\\sec^{-1}(x)$ where $x\\ge1$.<br /><br />(a) Compute $S(2)$.<br /><br />(b) Express $S(-x)$ in terms of $S(x)$.<br /><br />(c) Find the risk premium for $x=-2$.",
  "answeroption": "B",
  "explanation": "(a) Since $\\sec(\\pi/3)=2$, $S(2)=\\pi/3$. <br /><br />(b) Property: $\\sec^{-1}(-x)=\\pi-\\sec^{-1}(x)$. <br /><br />(c) $S(-2)=\\pi-\\pi/3=2\\pi/3$.",
  "explanation_image": [],
  "options": {
